cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Curb Cut's code or its public aggregates, please cite it as below.
  Cite the underlying surveys too (Nigeria DHS 2024, NBS MPI Survey 2021,
  GHS-Panel Waves 4 and 5); their citations are in docs/references.bib and in
  each data/public/*/README.md.
type: software
title: "Curb Cut: accessible open data on disability in Nigeria"
abstract: >-
  Code and disclosure-checked public aggregates for survey-weighted state
  disability prevalence in Nigeria (Nigeria DHS 2024, Washington Group Short
  Set), a pre-registered analysis of disability and multidimensional poverty
  (NBS MPI Survey 2021; an adjusted association, not a causal effect), an
  exploratory GHS-Panel two-wave comparison, and an accessible static site.
  Licensed microdata are not included.
authors:
  # Name and ORCID as given in the repository README ("Who's building it").
  # TODO(author): confirm the name form and ORCID, and add an affiliation if wanted.
  - family-names: Bannister
    given-names: Jerry
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3302-9558"
    alias: batestguy
repository-code: "https://github.com/batestguy/curb-cut"
url: "https://batestguy.github.io/curb-cut/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - disability
  - Nigeria
  - Washington Group Short Set
  - survey statistics
  - multidimensional poverty
  - double machine learning
  - statistical disclosure control
  - accessibility
references:
